questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot 3.2 microservice running on Java 21 was recently migrated to use Virtual Threads via `spring.threads.virtual.enabled=true`. Under heavy load, the service becomes completely unresponsive, CPU utilization plummets close to 0%, and thread dumps reveal that all carrier threads in `ForkJoinPool` are stuck in `WAITING` or `TIMED_WAITING`. You inspect the offending component:

java
@Component
public class CacheManager {
    private final Map<String, String> localCache = new HashMap<>();

    public synchronized String getOrFetch(String key, RemoteService remoteService) {
        if (!localCache.containsKey(key)) {
            String value = remoteService.blockingHttpFetch(key);
            localCache.put(key, value);
        }
        return localCache.get(key);
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an order processing system occasionally leaves the database in an inconsistent state. The method is annotated with `@Transactional`, but database writes dispatched inside asynchronous stages fail to roll back when downstream steps throw an exception, resulting in orphaned records:

java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    @Autowired private OrderRepository orderRepository;
    @Autowired private InventoryService inventoryService;

    @Transactional
    public CompletableFuture<Void> processOrder(Order order) {
        orderRepository.save(order);
        return CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> {
            inventoryService.reserveStock(order.getId());
            orderRepository.updateStatus(order.getId(), Status.PROCESSED);
        });
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an edge gateway running on Java 21 with Virtual Threads enabled shows severe thread starvation, latency spikes, and rejected requests under 10,000 concurrent requests, despite having plenty of free memory and low CPU usage. The endpoint code was written as follows:

java
@GetMapping("/aggregate/{id}")
public CompletableFuture<AggregatedResponse> aggregate(@PathVariable String id) {
    return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> userService.fetchBlocking(id))
        .thenCombine(
            CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> orderService.fetchBlocking(id)),
            (user, order) -> new AggregatedResponse(user, order)
        );
}
